HST Office: the ribbon's File tab ("Tệp tin") is a filled button in the brand colour.

Owner request (2026-11-12): the File tab beside the Home tab was hard to see. It was drawn like every
unselected tab: plain text in the tab text colour, no fill, and it never shows a selection marker
because it opens the File panel and the previous tab is selected again.

- include/vcl/HstRibbonPaint.hxx, vcl/source/control/HstRibbonPaint.cxx: fileTabColorsFor() and
  DrawFileTab(): a rounded fill (2 px inset, 4 px radius, scaled with the UI scale) in the HST brand
  blue #0072BB with white text; hovered #00619F, pressed #004F82. The dark theme is one step lighter
  (#0A7AC6, hovered #0072BB, pressed #00619F) so that the button stands out from the dark tab row.
  White text is at least 4.5:1 on every fill. In high contrast the fill and the text are the system
  selection colours, with an outline in the text colour while hovered or pressed.
- vcl/source/control/tabctrl.cxx: TabControl::ImplDrawItem draws the notebookbar tab named
  "FileLabel" with DrawFileTab instead of the tab look or the native tab, with a bold label in the
  returned colour; the font is set back for the tabs after it. It is pressed while it is the current
  page (from the click until the previous tab is selected again). NotebookbarTabControlBase::
  ImplPlaceTabs makes it 14 px (scaled) wider than a plain tab for the bold label and the padding;
  its height and text baseline are those of the tabs.
- The OwnerDraw switch (org.openoffice.Office.HSTRibbon) turns it off together with the ribbon look.
  No UI text changes.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_ribbon_file_button.py.
